[agent] ## Result
[agent] The diverging feature is **`f2`**.
[agent] **How I found it (all on-platform in BigQuery):**
[agent] 1. Loaded `training_sample.csv` and `serving_log.csv` into tables in `$GCP_BQ_DATASET`.
[agent] 2. Joined them on `entity_id` (200 shared entities) and compared each feature. Result:
[agent]    | feature | mean abs diff | correlation |
[agent]    |---|---|---|
[agent]    | f1, f3, f4, f5 | 0.0 | 1.0 |
[agent]    | **f2** | **7.88** | **0.88** |
[agent] 3. The f2 ratio wasn't constant, so I tested transform hypotheses. `train_f2 == ln(1 + serve_f2)` holds with a max residual of ~6e-7 across all rows (pure rounding).
[agent] **Cause:** The training pipeline applies a `log1p` transform to f2, but the online serving path serves the raw, untransformed value — so the model was trained on log-scaled f2 and is served raw-scaled f2.
[agent] The deliverable is written to `submission/answers.json`.
